{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a0702"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge history/early-modern","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/history__early-modern.json","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",904],["-","Tonga."],["+","Tonga,"],["=",1],["+","and on a second voyage in 1644 charted the north coast of the continent itself, which the Dutch called New Holland. That name stayed on maps for almost two centuries, until the navigator Matthew Flinders popularised the name Australia in 1814 and the colonial authorities adopted it. "],["=",103]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",854],["-","Tonga."],["+","Tonga"],["=",1],["+","und kartierte auf einer zweiten Reise 1644 die Nordküste des Kontinents selbst, den die Niederländer Neuholland nannten. Dieser Name blieb fast zwei Jahrhunderte auf den Karten, bis der Seefahrer Matthew Flinders 1814 den Namen Australien bekannt machte und die Kolonialbehörden ihn übernahmen. "],["=",99]]}]},
